164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In 2019, the Italian Parliament passed Law No. 69, known as the Codice Rosso, which introduced fast-track procedures for reporting gender-based violence, created new legal categories such as revenge porn, and increased penalties for domestic abuse [13]. Although not explicitly centered on femicide, the law can be considered a significant step forward in the fight against VaW, though its impact remains understudied. It offers a strategic chronological anchor to investigate whether media narratives around femicide shifted alongside this institutional momentum.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To explore this, we draw on the FMNews dataset on Italian femicide news coverage developed and presented by Cappuccio et al. [5]. While their work provides valuable descriptive insights into keyword patterns and semantic associations, our study adds a longitudinal and interpretive dimension by examining whether framing patterns in the press changed in the years surrounding the Codice Rosso.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
