/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (To assess how Italian media discourse around femicide has evolved along the introduction of Codice Rosso, we apply comparative methods from Natural Language Processing \(NLP\). Our study conceptualizes media language as both a reflection of and a contributor to cultural meaning-making [6]. Through NLP techniques, we quantify changes in framing by identifying lexical, grammatical, and emotional patterns across time.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We base our analysis on the FMNews-Nat corpus [5], a dataset of femicide-related articles published between 2009 and 2024 across six national newspapers with differing political orientations, which we do not disaggregate, as the focus of this study lies on broader patterns of media representation rather than outlet-specific variation. The full procedure for data extraction and cleaning is documented in the original FMNews dataset publication [5]. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
