194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Articles published after the Codice Rosso use structural keywords less frequently, dropping from approximately 2.0% to 1.6% of total words, while depoliticized keywords rise from 2.4% to just over 3% \(Figure 1\). The shift is statistically robust, with two-tailed t-tests yielding p < 0.0001 in both cases \(Table 1\). The consistent increase in depoliticized framing suggests that, contrary to our hypothesis, the discourse has not moved toward greater structural contextualization following the reform. Instead, media representations appear to have further individualized and      privatized      the      narrative     of     femicide.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [19 20]
>>
