207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Syntactic frame analysis evaluates how events are grammatically framed in media discourse, particularly in the attribution or suppression of agency [14]. This technique allows us to test whether Italian news coverage of femicide shifted toward more agentive framing following the Codice Rosso \(H2\). While Minnema et al. [14] employ a neural frame-semantic parser, we replicate their analytical logic using open-source NLP tools and rule-based syntactic modeling. We identify four event-based frames: Killing, Death, Cause_Harm, and Event, adapted from the framework developed by Minnema et al. [14], which maps grammatical patterns to the perceived distribution of agency in narratives of VaW. These capture how violence is linguistically constructed: whether it is framed as a deliberate act, a neutral occurrence, or an anonymized event. Their original study provides detailed examples for each frame, which informed our operationalisation [14]. To   detect    syntactic   framing,   we    define    three )
/E (Syntactic frame analysis evaluates how events are grammatically framed in media discourse, particularly in the attribution or suppression of agency [14]. This technique allows us to test whether Italian news coverage of femicide shifted toward more agentive framing following the Codice Rosso \(H2\). While Minnema et al. [14] employ a neural frame-semantic parser, we replicate their analytical logic using open-source NLP tools and rule-based syntactic modeling. We identify four event-based frames: Killing, Death, Cause_Harm, and Event, adapted from the framework developed by Minnema et al. [14], which maps grammatical patterns to the perceived distribution of agency in narratives of VaW. These capture how violence is linguistically constructed: whether it is framed as a deliberate act, a neutral occurrence, or an anonymized event. Their original study provides detailed examples for each frame, which informed our operationalisation [14]. To   detect    syntactic   framing,   we    define    three )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [14 15]
>>
